  nonce: 64c0  # 64c0
  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/iobcat2/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Re-checked 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e: rust.py still splits only _RUST_ABSOLUTE_PATH_ROOTS={std,core,alloc}. Fixture with Cargo.toml deps serde_json/tokio: `let r = serde_json::from_slice(..)` emits rust:external:0-0:serde_json..from_slice with dst_ref None (premise holds). But the item's own examples serde_json::from_str and tokio::fs::read emit NO edge at all: from_str/read are in SUPPRESSED_METHOD_NAMES['rust'] (INV-polad, 91a5b31813, 2026-08-24) and the guard drops an unbound denylisted leaf. A manifest-aware split would rescue those too (ext_ref set bypasses the guard). MECHANISM: rust external-call arm splits only std/core/alloc-rooted paths; crate heads are not recognised without Cargo.toml dependency names, and denylisted leaf names are then dropped outright. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-hajag."  # 64c0
